From 4d40ae88bf45d0a11229dc3bbc583862108422fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm: verisilicon: disable the primary plane correctly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The primary-plane disable callback sets FB_EN, exactly like its enable
callback.  Consequently the DC8200 continues scanning out the old buffer
after DRM has disabled the plane.  DRM may already have released or reused
the buffer.  This is visible on PineTab-V as stale characters, short-lived
image trails and corruption across fbcon-to-compositor and GNOME modeset
transitions.

The vendor DC8200 driver programs bit 13 from fb.enable and writes zero
when disabling a primary plane.  Mirror that behavior by clearing FB_EN
before committing the shadow registers.

Fixes: dbf21777caa8 ("drm: verisilicon: add a driver for Verisilicon display controllers")
Link: https://github.com/starfive-tech/linux/blob/pinetabv-6.6.y-devel/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_dc_hw.c
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_primary_plane.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_primary_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_primary_plane.c
index 9733abf79e06..719ca73b56d9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_primary_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/vs_primary_plane.c
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ static void vs_primary_plane_atomic_disable(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	unsigned int output = vcrtc->id;
 	struct vs_dc *dc = vcrtc->dc;
 
-	regmap_set_bits(dc->regs, VSDC_FB_CONFIG_EX(output),
-			VSDC_FB_CONFIG_EX_FB_EN);
+	regmap_clear_bits(dc->regs, VSDC_FB_CONFIG_EX(output),
+			  VSDC_FB_CONFIG_EX_FB_EN);
 
 	vs_primary_plane_commit(dc, output);
-- 
2.51.0
